1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,768
My dead brother just spoke to me through a broken radio.

2
00:00:04,068 --> 00:00:12,252
Leo died three years ago in a car crash. Yet his exact voice crackles from this dusty speaker right now.

3
00:00:12,552 --> 00:00:22,704
I press record. I need to capture the proof. The static shrieks back, burying his whispered warning underneath rising electronic noise.

4
00:00:23,004 --> 00:00:30,300
He says my name. He tells me to stop listening to the ghosts before the feedback loop consumes my entire mind.

5
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:39,552
I unplug the radio. Total silence fills the attic. But the voice doesn't stop. It echoes louder inside my skull.

6
00:00:39,852 --> 00:00:47,436
I touch my throat. It vibrates like a guitar string, humming with the exact radio frequency that Leo used.

7
00:00:47,736 --> 00:00:55,464
The waveform on my screen proves the truth. The audio isn't broadcasting into the room. It is coming straight from me.

8
00:00:55,764 --> 00:01:05,124
I am the transmitter. Every tear, every desperate midnight wish I whispered to his memory built this impossible machine.

9
00:01:05,424 --> 00:01:12,024
Leo never spoke to me. I simply learned how to mimic his ghost so I wouldn't have to face the quiet.

10
00:01:12,324 --> 00:01:18,276
If I am the one speaking the past into the dark, then who is listening to me right now?
